WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
Trace one release through nine handoffs.

00:00:02.448 --> 00:00:05.920
This is AI assistance to an existing
payments testing team,

00:00:05.973 --> 00:00:08.480
distinct from evaluating
an AI application.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:13.280
Start with approved context:
the payment story, API contract

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.440
and relevant defects.
AI drafts clarification questions.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.760
Product and domain QA approve
the rule that a same-key,

00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:26.853
same-payload retry returns the original
transfer without a second posting.

00:00:27.301 --> 00:00:30.240
Next, test design produces
a reviewed matrix.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.920
AI proposes timeout, duplicate callback,

00:00:33.987 --> 00:00:37.080
concurrency and conflicting-payload cases.

00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:42.200
Domain QA supplies the expected behavior
independently of the implementation.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.480
A written case is an input to executable
test code, not the code itself.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.280
The developer unit-test step uses
the handler source and accepted behavior.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.720
Copilot can draft JUnit candidates for key
validation and duplicate-request logic.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.400
The developer checks the fake
repository and verifies

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:04.080
one insertion for repeated
calls. A passing unit test

00:01:04.176 --> 00:01:07.733
does not establish correctness across
the real database and provider.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.720
The API and user-interface step turns
the reviewed matrix into a pull request.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.480
REST Assured tests exercise
the payment service;

00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:21.000
selected Playwright checks cover the
customer's pending state and retry action.

00:01:21.074 --> 00:01:24.960
Reviewers require the original
transfer identifier, one journal,

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.560
and balances of ninety thousand
and ten thousand minor units.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.880
A status-only assertion is rejected.

00:01:31.552 --> 00:01:34.560
Data and provider behavior
are versioned inputs.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.160
AI can draft synthetic seed scripts and
WireMock mappings for acceptance followed

00:01:40.187 --> 00:01:44.640
by a timeout. Engineers validate those
mappings against the provider contract.

00:01:44.768 --> 00:01:48.880
Testcontainers and the delivery
pipeline supply repeatable resources.

00:01:49.072 --> 00:01:52.680
Real-provider and settlement checks
remain separate requirements.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.840
For execution, AI may recommend
affected tests or request an authorized

00:01:57.893 --> 00:02:02.560
pipeline job. Azure Pipelines runs
the approved suite and publishes raw

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:08.160
JUnit results and traces. The mandatory
payment suite cannot be silently omitted.

00:02:08.286 --> 00:02:10.880
Record the build, test commit,

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.480
fixture and stub versions
under the run identifier.

00:02:14.846 --> 00:02:19.800
During investigation, AI reads
retained evidence and proposes a cause.

00:02:19.947 --> 00:02:24.400
In our injected-defect example, the
assertion expects one journal but observes

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.280
two. The defect draft
must link that evidence.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.480
A reviewer confirms the diagnosis,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.280
and the original failing
verdict remains unchanged.

00:02:33.481 --> 00:02:37.961
For repair, AI may propose a source
change for developer review.

00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:40.321
Keep the accepted
payment assertions fixed.

00:02:40.481 --> 00:02:45.601
The pipeline uses a fresh run identifier
and isolated data for the retest.

00:02:45.821 --> 00:02:48.481
The corrected build must pass,

00:02:48.521 --> 00:02:51.801
and the deliberate duplicate-posting
variant must still fail.

00:02:52.041 --> 00:02:55.601
For release evidence,
AI drafts a summary of coverage,

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:59.481
run results, reviewed
dispositions and missing checks.

00:02:59.591 --> 00:03:04.081
The release owner reviews the linked pack,
including required real-provider evidence.

00:03:04.205 --> 00:03:08.441
Accepted defects can become
reviewed regression cases.

00:03:08.531 --> 00:03:11.361
The shared platform
provides context access,

00:03:11.405 --> 00:03:15.041
artifact versions, scoped
pipeline access and evidence

00:03:15.097 --> 00:03:18.961
retention across these steps;
it does not replace the named owners.
